  "narrative": "None of the newly delivered wave-3 comparisons meets the acceptance bar for a scientifically meaningful association in the hypothesized direction. Acceptance would require a signed 95% interval lower bound clearly above the approximate 10% relative scale threshold: about 0.025 for outcome_004 and outcome_016, and about 0.028 for outcome_008. No direct claim satisfies this. For H15 and H19, the signed upper bounds (about 0.024 and 0.023) are below the approximate outcome_004 threshold, so the maximum clinically meaningful effect in the claimed direction is not supported; I rejected those directional claims and closed them. These rejections are directional: they do not exclude an opposite effect, but reversing post hoc would be data-driven and would worsen multiplicity. H14, H16, H17, and H20 remain unresolved: their point estimates are below threshold and intervals include zero, but the upper bounds exceed the approximate clinical threshold, so I cannot reject them outright. I kept H17 active because it is the strongest direct near-threshold signal (outcome_008, feature_002 within feature_008=1), and deferred H14/H16/H20 to avoid overextending on weak context-specific estimates. The interaction H24 is the strongest heterogeneity signal: outcome_008 feature_002 contrast is nominally about 0.048 signed units larger in the feature_008=1 subgroup than in the feature_008=0 complement, above the point threshold, but its interval still includes zero and is wide because the complement cells are smaller. I kept H24 active rather than accepting or rejecting it. Interactions H21, H22, and H23 are much weaker and/or include zero; I deferred H21 but closed H22 and H23 as heterogeneity follow-ups. I did not request validation this iteration because no direct claim is strong enough that an independent interval, which will be more conservative after accounting for the maximum number of validations, is likely to convert the current evidence into acceptance. Instead, I registered three focused complement mean-difference tests to characterize whether the near-signal direct effects and H24 interaction are localized: outcome_008 feature_002 in feature_008=0, outcome_016 feature_034 in feature_002=0, and outcome_008 feature_002 in feature_034=0. These are observational associations in the supplied dataset only; predictor labels are opaque, correlated outcomes and confounding remain possible, and causal or generalizable claims are not supported.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted claims: none. Wave-3 results: H15 and H19 rejected because signed upper bounds fall below the approximate 10% outcome-scale threshold for outcome_004. H14/H16/H17/H20 remain unresolved because intervals include zero and upper bounds cross threshold; H17 active, others deferred. Interactions: H24 strongest but unresolved and active; H21 deferred; H22/H23 closed. H15 and H18 closed as duplicates/unsupported. Do not request validation unless a direct signed interval becomes strong enough that an independent interval has a reasonable chance to exceed threshold, or an interaction becomes strong enough to justify accepting heterogeneity without a direct effect. Current plan: test complementary contexts for feature_002 and feature_034 near-signals to see whether effects are localized or generalizable. Maintain strict directionality: feature_002 raw negative means stronger dependency; feature_034 raw positive means weaker dependency; signed estimates are already aligned to claim direction. All claims remain dataset-specific and noncausal.",
